b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays whose bounds are computed at run time (5.2.4.2), procedures and Boolean function designators (5.4), the Boolean operator of negation (3.4), the for statement (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), facts as arrays of integer codes (systems file, Values), and the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: S s1 ... sS M m1 ... mM T p1 k1 ... pT kT, the facts of the closed world: S and the atom of each fact student(s), M and the atom of each fact maths(m), T and the two atoms of each fact takes(p, k), each in order. Atoms are integer codes: brown 1, smith 2, c101 101, c301 301, any other atom another positive integer;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P06e3. The query nonmajor(p) with p unknown, by the one case of nonmajor: nonmajor(p) if student(p) and maths(k) and not takes(p, k), the conjuncts in that order. student, maths and takes are given by their facts. student(p) gives p the value of each fact in order, maths(k) gives k the value of each fact in order, and takes(p, k), with both known, is tested on its facts. Each derivation is reported as one answer, the value of p;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, ns, nm, nt;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constants: each relation's facts, their number first, which sizes its array;
  ns := read;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ st[1:ns];
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ ns d̲o̲ st[i] := read;
  nm := read;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ mt[1:nm];
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nm d̲o̲ mt[i] := read;
  nt := read;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ nm1, stud, math, tak, negs, found;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ tp, tk[1:nt];

  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ takes(p, c);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p, c; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p, c;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ takes(p, c) with both known: true when one of its facts is takes(p, c), in a closed world;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ t;
    t := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nt d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ tp[j] = p ∧ tk[j] = c t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ tak := tak + 1; t := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    takes := t
  e̲n̲d̲ takes;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printatom(a);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an atom, by its name if it is one of the problem's, else by its code;
  i̲f̲ a = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`brown') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ a = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`smith')
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ a = 101 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`c101') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ a = 301 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`c301')
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ print(a);

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ nonmajor;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ nonmajor(p) with p unknown, by its one case, the conjuncts in order. Each derivation is one answer;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a, b, p, kv;
    nm1 := nm1 + 1;
    f̲o̲r̲ a := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ ns d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      p := st[a]; stud := stud + 1;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        f̲o̲r̲ b := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nm d̲o̲
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
          kv := mt[b]; math := math + 1;
          negs := negs + 1;
          i̲f̲ ¬takes(p, kv) t̲h̲e̲n̲
          b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
            found := found + 1;
            PRINTTEXT(`[answer]p = '); printatom(p); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
          e̲n̲d̲
        e̲n̲d̲
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ nonmajor;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nt d̲o̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ tp[i] := read; tk[i] := read e̲n̲d̲;
  nm1 := stud := math := tak := negs := found := 0;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the query: nonmajor(p);
  nonmajor;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: whether there is a solution, and the applications of each relation;
  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  i̲f̲ found = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`each negation decided with p and k known'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations nonmajor/1 '); print(nm1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations student-facts-matched '); print(stud); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations maths-facts-matched '); print(math); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations takes-facts-matched '); print(tak); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations negations-decided '); print(negs); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
